WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.000
-I love having you on.
I have so much --

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.267
I like the -- I thought you were
going in for a double kiss.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:06.701
-I know.
I just did a single kiss.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.200
-Yeah, but it was
a good single kiss,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.934
but I thought you were
going for the second,

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.434
so I kind of waited
for the second.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.734
-I kind of messed up your beard
just a little bit right there.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.367
You might need your comb.
-Because it's fa-- Oh.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.100
-Is it fake?
-Thank you so much.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.033
It's fake.
-How did you grow that?

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.834
-I've been -- Spirit Halloween
opened down the street from me.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.000
[ Jazz music plays ]
And I --

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.434
-Is there music that plays
when you comb your beard?

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.367
-No, it's just in --
-Wow.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.467
-Wow. Yeah.
Big time. Big time, right?

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:34.200
No. Speaking of big time, I want
to talk to you about this.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.501
This is giant.
I wish that I did this.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.501
You went to the White House
just -- and saw --

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:39.534
-Yes.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:40.834
-Was it yesterday
or two days ago?

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:42.467
-Friday night.
-You saw Elton John's --

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.467
-We saw Elton John.
-At the White House.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.934
-Yes.
-How -- What was it like?

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.267
-It was crazy!

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.467
I mean, we grew up
listening to Elton John.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.167
I'm sure you did, too.
-Of course. I love Elton John.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.601
-So my mom called and was like,

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.033
"We're invited to the White
House. We should go back."

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.033
-But you are invited
always to the White House.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.901
-No, we're not.
No. We're not.

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:02.367
[ Laughter ]
-You grew up there.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.367
-Yeah, but you only are there
for a brief period,

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.100
and then you can't go back.
-I understand.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.300
You can't just ring the doorbell
and be like, "I have the key."

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.868
-No, and in fact, when we
walked out, my husband goes,

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.100
"Don't you wish we were just
going upstairs to go to bed?"

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.801
-Really?
-We had to be like, "Okay.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.834
Now time to go to the hotel."
-No. You have to leave.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.667
You're like, "No,
we don't live here anymore."

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:21.167
-"It's time to go."
-Wow.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.100
-But it was very cool to see
Elton John on the South Lawn.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.000
And I took my little girls,
who had never been,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.868
and they couldn't believe it.
-I have a photo.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.000
-They were like, "Wait. What?"
-They couldn't be cuter.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.534
Look at them here.
-They're they are.

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:31.701
-Come on.
-Yes.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.400
-Stop it right now.
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.868
But what a great family.

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.901
But here's what I want --
I have a photo here.

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:37.968
But this made me laugh.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.000
You brought this
exclusive for us.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.300
-I sure did.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.868
-This is taken
by President Biden.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.334
-President Biden took a picture.

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:47.133
First of all,
they were so gracious.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.734
They met us at the front gate.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.834
-You know, like, we drove in
like we used to,

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.634
and they met us there.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.467
They were standing on the steps,
and my kids were like,

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.834
[ Gasps ]
"That's the President?!

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.133
What do we do?!"

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.033
And I'm like "You say,
'Hello, Mr. President.'"

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:04.067
And Mila's like,
"What if I was like,

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.934
'Hey. I'm Mila.
What's your name?'"

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.334
I'm like,
"Then you'll never come back."

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.033
-"No! Don't you --
Don't you ever do that.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.234
Don't even joke around."
-"Then you'll never come back."

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.968
But, yeah, he was --

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.634
-But not only that,
but he took a photo.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.567
-He was like -- There
was a portrait of my mom...

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.934
-Of course.
-...hanging on the wall.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.267
-In the White House.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.601
-And he said,
"Can I get a picture?"

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.934
Which is just the sweetest.
-I love this.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.601
And here's the photo right here.
-...took the picture.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:26.968
-Look at this. The pic --

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.267
The portrait not even close
to being in the shot.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.734
Barely.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.467
That's your --
That's your mom's arms.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:37.267
That's her arms.
Or is it her dre-- Yeah.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.501
-I mean,
look at everybody's face.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.901
It's also some, like --
some sort of talking.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:46.067
I think --
-She's so cute. She's so cute.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.634
Everyone's talking.
You're looking somewhere else.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.801
-I'm pretty sure what I said is,

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:54.868
"President Biden, my husband
can take the picture."

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.367
We didn't really expect
the President...

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.901
-You have to frame this.
-...to take it.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.400
-The President took this photo.
-I know.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.434
-You have to frame this.
-It was very gracious of him.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.901
-And I didn't get to
see you the other night.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.767
I know you were
at Harry Styles...

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:06.934
-Yes.
-...at the Garden.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.501
-How good was it?
-He's unbelievable.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.133
-Wait. Can I just tell you --

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:13.300
Jimmy, I know where you were
'cause I was right above you.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.400
-How did --

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.667
-First of all,
people were walking by.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:19.167
I was like, "Is that Olivia
Wilde? Who is sitting there?"

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.767
Because people were waving
at this one person.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.501
And it was you!
-Yeah.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:27.033
-The millennial girls
know and love you!

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.701
-Yeah, that's my fanbase.
-It must be.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.300
I kind of saw him.
-No, no, no.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.601
They sat me in these seats
with, like, spotlights on me

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.234
for some reason.
-I saw it.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.968
-I go, "Any other seat
is totally fine.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.801
I just want to see Harry
and have a good time

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:45.100
and kind of just dance."
-Yeah. Your dance moves, too.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.234
I mean, I was watching Harry
most of the time because, wow.

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.501
-Who doesn't watch Harry Styles?
-Right?

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.901
-Yeah.
-Harry Styles.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.300
-My dance moves were a little...

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.167
-But he -- Jimmy does some major
sort of, like --

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.734
It's like Grateful Dead
meets Dad dancing.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.501
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.100
What are you talking about?
-You were, like, jamming out.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.801
-Kind of jamming out?
I wasn't doing that.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:07.133
-Yeah, you totally were.
-I tried -- Like a ski thing?

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.734
I was trying different --
I was trying different moves

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.400
because I was embarrassed
because I was Dad dancing.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.400
But I was Dad dancing
before I was a dad.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.968
That's how I dance.
-No, I know.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.901
I Mom danced before I was a mom.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:20.701
-And I'm, like, dancing,
and I go -- And all these --

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:22.200
-Girls. I saw it.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.501
-They had all their phones out,
and I'm already a meme.

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.334
I go, "Alright.
This is already a disaster."

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.734
I was, like, trying to be that.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.167
And then I'm like,
"Maybe I'll clap."

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.868
-Oh, you were doing
sort of a side clap.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.234
-I was side clapping.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.434
Then I --
That wasn't really working.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.367
And then I go,
"I got to stop side clapping."

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.367
And then I just stood there,
and then I did this for a bit.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:46.167
And I go, "How creepy is that?"
I go, "I just got to stop."

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:47.934
And then I go,
"I'm just gonna have fun."

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.334
-Wait, but also weren't you

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.834
singing every word
to every song?

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.334
Like, at one point,
I thought to myself...

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:56.167
-That's so sad.
-..."If my children were here,

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:57.667
they would be --
they would have left."

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.934
-Yeah.
-They would have been so

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:00.834
humiliated because I knew --
-You can't look cool

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.367
at a concert.
-No, we're nerds.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.834
-I love him.
I love Harry Styles.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:05.367
That's why I sang
every song I knew.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:07.234
I'm like -- Love it.
"Matilda."

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:10.000
-Oh, "Matilda" is so good.
-Don't even talk to me.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.834
-"Matilda"!
-"Matilda" is the jam.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.767
-"Matilda" is so good.
"Late Night Talking." Ooh.

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.267
-I was doing all of it.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.567
-My 3-year-old son can sing
"Late Night Talking."

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.634
-He knows all the words?
-Yeah, he's like -- ♪ Talking ♪

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.400
-Does Hoda --
Does Hoda get into Harry?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.200
-Oh, Hoda loves Harry.
-She does?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.901
-We actually -- Harry played
on the "Today" show,

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:30.133
and he smells
like you think he smells.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.968
-Yeah.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.467
Like, you know what I mean?

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.334
-That's all I wanted to hear.
-Just like you think he smells.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.801
-That's all we wanted to hear.
He does, right?

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.167
-Whew. Yes.
-Yeah, he's money in the bank.

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:39.467
-I mean, what is it
about Harry Styles?

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:41.334
-He's money. He's just got it.
-We can't help it.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:44.133
-He's got it. He's just got
everything. He's so cool.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.968
I want to talk to you
about your book club.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:48.934
Because this is a giant deal, by
the way, buddy. Congratulations.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.767
-Oh, thank you.
-It's a massive hit.

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:52.200
"Read with Jenna."

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.534
I want to say --
You do a book a month.

00:05:54.534 --> 00:05:56.400
-Yes.
-And out of -- out of the ones

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.868
you've done, 33 have hit

00:05:57.868 --> 00:05:59.200
"The New York Times"
Best Seller list.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.133
-Wow. You did your homework.
-I did do my homework.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:02.367
Yeah, I don't need --
-Yeah.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.934
-I don't need this.
This is all fake.

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.000
I don't need any of this stuff.
I know who I'm talking to.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.267
-I know. It's --
-I'm a big fan.

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.567
But congratulations.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.133
-Well, and you kind of
have a book club, too.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:12.067
We need to do a collab.
-I would do a collab.

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:14.167
-Do you wanna do a collab?
-I would love to do one.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.400
I don't --
-You're starting. Right?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.267
-We were doing summer book club.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:19.534
-I think you gotta do more.
-Really?

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.367
Because here's the thing.

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:22.901
There are a ton of readers
out there.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.567
-There are.
-And there's tons of authors.

00:06:24.567 --> 00:06:27.367
Our mission is to highlight
debuting diverse authors

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:30.334
to give authors that haven't
always had, like,

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:32.701
the money behind them a platform
in the "Today" show.

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:33.968
-Yeah.
-And it's been awesome.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.567
-And you've done it.
-It's awesome. It's so fun.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.000
-You've done
what you wanted to achieve.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.200
You've achieved a goal,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.000
and it's continuing
to get bigger and bigger.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.100
And I just heard that you
started a production company.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.601
-Yes.
-What is it called?

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:45.067
-Well, Thousand Voices.
-Thousand Voices.

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:47.567
-We're almost there,
but we can tell you,

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:50.100
and the point is to have a ton
of different perspectives.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.300
-yeah.
-I feel like --

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.767
-And you're going to make them
into movies?

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:53.934
-And television shows.

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.267
So, we have seven projects
right now...

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:57.334
-This is massive for people.
-...of books that I love

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.667
that hopefully some of you all
have read with us

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:01.100
that will one day
be on the screen

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.934
if we can get our act together.
-Congratulations.

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:04.367
-But it feels really good
to people.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:05.734
-It's cool
that you're doing this.

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:07.767
And it's like, yeah, get
more people out there reading.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:08.868
-Yes.
-I love it, love it, love it.

00:07:08.868 --> 00:07:10.300
-Yes, yes.
-You're awesome, pal.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.501
I love you.
-Thank you.

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:13.067
-Jenna Bush Hager, everybody.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:16.467
Catch "Today with Hoda &amp; Jenna"
